        "comments": "The assembly lpCarNigr3.hap1.1 is based on 51x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The region of Chromosome 22 from start to 2.3 Mbp appears to be collapsed by the assembler and should be represented in two copy but is only present in single copy in this assembly. The following regions appear to be haplotypic inversions: Chromosome 22\n0.2-0.9 Mbp, Chromosome 10\n2.7-6.2 Mbp. Chromosome B1 is a putative B chromosome.",
